-- title:
--   Fact (i), p.26 — exchange lies in the commutant of the collective spin
-- statement:
--   Let $E_{ab}$ be the exchange of qubits $a\neq b$ of an $n$-qubit register and $S_\alpha=\sum_j\sigma^j_\alpha$ the collective operators. Then
--   1. $E_{ab}$ commutes with $S_x$, $S_y$ and $S_z$;
--   2. $E_{ab}$ commutes with the total Casimir $(s^n)^2$;
--   3. $E_{ab}$ maps every eigenspace of $s_z$ into itself, so exchange "does not change the value of $m_J$";
--   4. every element of the real Lie algebra $\mathfrak g_n$ generated by the $iE_{ab}$ commutes with every $S_\alpha$.
--
--   This is why exchange can act on the DFSs at all: anything built from it respects the decomposition (7.1) and acts only on the multiplicity index.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: qubits 1, …, n; |0⟩, |1⟩ → 0-based wires Fin n; Bool basis with false = |0⟩; reason: Lean convention; same operators
--   - generalization: the exchange operators are in the commutant of {S_α} and do not change m_J → also commute with (s^n)², and every element of the generated real Lie algebra commutes with the S_α; reason: the added clauses follow from the printed commutation and are what the proof uses; the printed clauses are clauses 1 and 3
-- source:
--   Kempe, Bacon, Lidar & Whaley, Theory of Decoherence-Free Fault-Tolerant Universal Quantum Computation, arXiv:quant-ph/0004064v2, fact (i), §VII.D, p.26

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_exchangeLie
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_partialCasimir
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_szEigenspace

open QAlgorithms

namespace CollectiveDFS

/-- Fact (i) of the proof of Theorem 5 (Kempe, Bacon, Lidar & Whaley, arXiv:quant-ph/0004064v2, §VII.D, p.26, PDF p.26): "The exchange operators do
not change the value of m_J, because they are in the commutant of A = {S_α}". For wires `a ≠ b`,
`E_ab` commutes with `S_x, S_y, S_z` and with the total Casimir `(s^n)²`, and maps every
`s_z`-eigenspace into itself; and every element of the real Lie algebra generated by the `i E_ab`
commutes with every `S_α`.

**Formalization Note** `α : Fin 3` with `0, 1, 2 = x, y, z`; `S_α = partialS n n α`; doubled
magnetic label `m2 = 2m`; wires 0-based. -/
theorem exchange_commute_collective (n : ℕ) :
    (∀ a b : Fin n, a ≠ b → ∀ α : Fin 3, Commute (exchange a b) (partialS n n α)) ∧
    (∀ a b : Fin n, a ≠ b → Commute (exchange a b) (partialCasimir n n)) ∧
    (∀ a b : Fin n, a ≠ b → ∀ m2 : ℤ, ∀ ψ ∈ szEigenspace n m2,
      Matrix.toEuclideanLin (exchange a b) ψ ∈ szEigenspace n m2) ∧
    (∀ X ∈ exchangeLie n, ∀ α : Fin 3, Commute X (partialS n n α)) := by sorry

end CollectiveDFS
